# src/packages/control-ui

## Purpose
Canonical authored React/Vite control UI plus a checked fail-closed bootstrap; CI/release builds replace dist/ with the production bundle.

## Contents
- Direct files (13): `.gitignore`, `.oxlintrc.json`, `README.md`, `embed.go`, `embed_test.go`, `go.mod`, `index.html`, `package-lock.json`, `package.json`, `tsconfig.app.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `tsconfig.node.json` …
- Child folders: `scripts/`, `src/`.
- `dist/` is a checked fail-closed bootstrap that CI/release replaces with generated output; `public/` contains copied static assets. Neither receives nested `.context` files to avoid changing bundle contents.

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `controlui`.
- Notable exported surface: `Dist`.
- Daemon-local dependencies: none.
- Direct daemon callers: none detected.

## Invariants
- This is the sole authored control UI; desktop/daemon hosts consume its canonical bundle rather than forking UI source.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
